<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Potash downgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Potash downgraded.</headline>
<text>
<p>- EVEREN Securities Inc said Tuesday it lowered its short-term rating on Potash Corp of Saskatchewan to underperformer from market performer because of the company's proposed acquisition of Arcadian Corp.</p>
<p>- The firm said its long-term rating of Potash remains a market performer.  </p>
<p>- Potash said it planned to acquire Arcadian, a leading producer of nitrogen fertilizer. With the acquisition, Potash becomes a fully integrated fertilizer company.</p>
<p>- EVEREN said Arcadian was in a commodity business. Nitrogen producers are subject to volatile and unpredictable raw material prices for natural gas and ammonia, it said.</p>
<p>- Potash fell three to 100.50 in Toronto and 2-3/4 to 73-1/4 on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
